course: dictionary
lesson: 4031
title: Gauze: a thin cloth with tiny holes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When you meet a new word, look at the words around it for clues. «When a baby tooth comes out and the gap bleeds, biting on clean gauze (a soft cloth pad) or tissue for a few minutes stops it.» The brackets tell you what gauze is: a soft cloth pad.
explain: Gauze is a very thin, light cloth with tiny holes in it. It is also a fine net made of wire, which is used in science equipment. The sentence tells you which meaning is which: a soft cloth pad for a bleeding gap, and a net when the word is about wire.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «biting on clean cloth pad» instead of «biting on clean gauze»: it still makes sense, so your idea is right. If you are not sure, a dictionary will settle it.
fact: Gauze is a very thin, light cloth with tiny holes in it.
fact: A gauze pad is a soft cloth pad that can be used to cover a cut or scrape.
fact: «Gauze» is a noun, and you can say some gauze, or a gauze pad or gauze bandage.
fact: «Wire gauze» is a fine net of wire, used in science equipment.
fact: Context clues, such as the words in brackets, can tell you which meaning of a word the writer means.
exercise: «When a baby tooth comes out and the gap bleeds, biting on clean gauze (a soft cloth pad) or tissue for a few minutes stops it.» What is gauze in this sentence? | *A soft cloth pad | A type of tooth | A hard plastic cup | A sweet to suck
exercise: Mia says her cut needs a gauze pad. What is a gauze pad for? | *To cover a cut and keep it clean | To hang on a wall as a decoration | To carry water to school | To catch rain in the garden
exercise: In science, the teacher puts «wire gauze» on a tripod. What is wire gauze? | A glass jar | *A fine net of wire | A thick wooden board | A cloth bandage
test: Gauze is a very thin, light cloth with what? | Thick walls | Sharp points | Bright colours | *Tiny holes
test: Which phrase means a fine net made of wire? | Soft cloth | *Wire gauze | Clean tissue | Gauze pad
exam: Ella sees «gauze» on the first aid box. What does it mean? | *A very thin, light cloth with tiny holes | A small glass bottle | A hard plastic cup | A type of sweet
